      <li style="list-style: none"><h2>DataVis PhD Stuff</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><h3>Writing</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><a href="thesaurus.com/">Thesaurus</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://www.powerthesaurus.org/">Power Thesaurus 🦖⚡</a></li>
              <li>low level rules <a href="https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~tmm/writing.html">https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~tmm/writing.html</a></li>
              <li>At a higher level, see the <a href="https://www.biorxiv.org/content/early/2017/05/23/088278">Ten Simple Rules for Structuring Papers (Kording and Mensh, PLOS Computational Biology)</a></li>
              <li>Useful Regex commands: 
                <code>
grep " an [^AEIOUaeiuo\\]" main.tex     # find wrong articles
grep " a [AEIOUaeiuo\\]" main.tex       # find wrong articles

egrep "(\b[a-zA-Z]+) \1\b" main.tex     # double words

egrep "(et\. al)|(et al[^\.])" main.tex # et al spelled wrongly
egrep "\s\\\\cite{'{'}" main.tex            # cite without nbsp
egrep "\w+, \w+ and " main.tex          # find missing oxford comma 
egrep "\w+, \w+, and " main.tex         # find oxford commas

grep "[^.][^A-Z]\. [a-z]" main.text     # Missing capital for first word in new sentence
                </code>
              </li>

              <li>How to write a scientific paper: <a href="https://www.cg.tuwien.ac.at/resources/HowToWriteAScientificPaper.html">https://www.cg.tuwien.ac.at/resources/HowToWriteAScientificPaper.html</a></li>
              <li>Common mistakes in technical writing: <a href="https://cs.dartmouth.edu/~wjarosz/writing.html">https://cs.dartmouth.edu/~wjarosz/writing.html</a></li>
              <li>Practical Tips and Tricks for Paper Writing (updated 2020): <a href="https://www.cg.tuwien.ac.at/research/publications/2010/groeller-2010-PTT/">https://www.cg.tuwien.ac.at/research/publications/2010/groeller-2010-PTT/</a></li>
              <li>Google Documentation Style Guide: <a href="https://developers.google.com/style/">https://developers.google.com/style/</a></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
